{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 5, 4]], "date-time": "2026-05-04T12:38:36Z", "timestamp": 1777898316720, "version": "3.51.4"}, "reference-count": 42, "publisher": "Wiley", "issue": "4", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 9, 24]], "date-time": "2024-09-24T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1727136000000}, "content-version": "am", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, {"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 9, 24]], "date-time": "2024-09-24T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1727136000000}, "content-version": "vor", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, {"start": {"date-parts": [[2024, 9, 24]], "date-time": "2024-09-24T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1727136000000}, "content-version": "tdm", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://doi.wiley.com/10.1002/tdm_license_1.1"}], "funder": [{"DOI": "10.13039/501100014825", "name": "Biotechnology Industry Research Assistance Council", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["BIRAC/TG/USAID/08/2014"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["BIRAC/TG/USAID/08/2014"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/501100014825", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/100000200", "name": "United States Agency for International Development", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["AID\u2010OAA\u2010A\u201013\u201000008"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["AID\u2010OAA\u2010A\u201013\u201000008"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/100000200", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}, {"DOI": "10.13039/100005825", "name": "National Institute of Food and Agriculture", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "award": ["WNP00449"], "award-info": [{"award-number": ["WNP00449"]}], "id": [{"id": "10.13039/100005825", "id-type": "DOI", "asserted-by": "publisher"}]}], "content-domain": {"domain": ["acsess.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"], "crossmark-restriction": true}, "short-container-title": ["The Plant Genome"], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2024, 12]]}, "abstract": "<jats:title>Abstract</jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    With every 1\u00b0C rise in temperature, yields are predicted to decrease by 5%\u20136% for both cool and warm season crops, threatening food production, which should double by 2050 to meet the global demand. While high night\u2010time temperature (HNT) stress is expected to increase due to climate change, limited information is available on the genetic control of the trait, especially in wheat (\n                    <jats:italic>Triticum aestivum</jats:italic>\n                    L.). To identify genes controlling the HNT trait, we evaluated a doubled haploid (DH) population developed from a cross between an HNT tolerant line KSG1203 and KSG0057, a selection out of a mega variety PBW343 from South East Asia that turned out to be HNT susceptible. The population, along with the parents, were evaluated under 30\u00b0C night\u2010time (HNT stress) keeping the daytime temperature to normal 22\u00b0C. The same daytime and 16\u00b0C night\u2010time temperature were used as a control. The HNT treatment negatively impacted all agronomic traits under evaluation, with a percentage reduction of 0.5%\u201335% for the tolerant parent, 8%\u201375% for the susceptible parent, and 8%\u201350% for the DH population. Performed using sequencing\u2010based genotyping, quantitative trait locus (QTL) mapping identified 19 QTLs on 13 wheat chromosomes explaining 9.72%\u201328.81% of cumulative phenotypic variance for HNT stress tolerance, along with 13 that were for traits under normal growing conditions. The size of QTL intervals ranged between 0.021 and 97.48 Mb, with the number of genes ranging between 2 and 867. A candidate gene analysis for the smallest six QTL intervals identified eight putative candidates for night\u2010time heat stress tolerance.\n                  </jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1002/tpg2.20517", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2024, 9, 25]], "date-time": "2024-09-25T10:30:15Z", "timestamp": 1727260215000}, "update-policy": "https://doi.org/10.1002/crossmark_policy", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 5, "title": ["Identification and mapping of QTLs and their corresponding candidate genes controlling high night\u2010time temperature stress tolerance in wheat (\n                    <i>Triticum aestivum</i>\n                    L.)"], "prefix": "10.1002", "volume": "17", "author": [{"given": "Kaviraj S.", "family": "Kahlon", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Crop and Soil Sciences Washington State University  Pullman Washington USA"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Kanwardeep S.", "family": "Rawale", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Geneshifters LLC  Pullman Washington USA"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"given": "Sachin", "family": "Kumar", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Botany/Department of Genetics and Plant Breeding Chaudhary Charan Singh University  Meerut Uttar Pradesh India"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}, {"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7370-6184", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Kulvinder S.", "family": "Gill", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [{"name": "Department of Crop and Soil Sciences Washington State University  Pullman Washington USA"}], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "311", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2024, 9, 24]]}, "reference": [{"key": "e_1_2_10_2_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.2135/cropsci2013.11.0793"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_3_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1126/science.aar7191"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_4_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1093/bioinformatics/btm308"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_5_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1093/bioinformatics/btg112"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_6_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1104/pp.112.207753"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_7_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1093/bioinformatics/btr330"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_8_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.3389/fpls.2014.00657"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_9_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/978-3-030-90673-3_4"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_10_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00222081"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_11_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1093/mp/sss119"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_12_1", "unstructured": "Hannon G. J.(2010).FASTX\u2010toolkit.https://github.com/agordon/fastx_toolkit"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_13_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1111/pce.12957"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_14_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1101/gr.9.9.868"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_15_1", "volume-title": "Climate change 2023: Synthesis report. Contribution of working groups I, II and III to the sixth assessment report of the Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change", "author": "IPCC", "year": "2023"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_16_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.3389/fpls.2016.01774"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_17_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1104/pp.19.00642"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_18_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1093/bioinformatics/btu031"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_19_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.3389/fpls.2021.712167"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_20_1", "article-title": "Physical map of QTLs for some agronomic traits across many environments, identification of related candidate genes, and development of KASP markers with emphasis on terminal heat stress tolerance in common wheat", "author": "Kumar S.", "year": "2024", "journal-title": "Research Square"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_21_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/s11032\u2010021\u201001264\u20107"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_22_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/nmeth.1923"}, {"key": "e_1_2_10_23_1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1111/j.1439\u20100523.1991.tb